Proposed addition to https://nouveau.freedesktop.org/DumpingVideoBios.html
(sources/DumpingVideoBios.mdwn on gitlab.freedesktop.org/nouveau/wiki)

Insert this section after the powerpc/Open Firmware block, before the
"Make sure you have a file..." paragraph:

------------------------------------------------------------------------

On EFI-booted Apple machines (e.g. MacBookPro4,1 / GeForce 8600M GT) none of
the usual sources work: the card has no option ROM, the `0xC0000` shadow area
is empty, the PCI ROM BAR reads as all-zero, and PRAMIN/PROM/ACPI/PLATFORM all
fail.  The VBIOS is stored inside a compressed UEFI firmware-file section in
the machine's SPI flash.  The flash contents are decoded into physical memory
below 4 GB via the ACPI INT0800 firmware-hub device, so the VBIOS can be
recovered by mapping that window (e.g. with a read-only MTD map driver or
flashrom) and scanning the firmware volumes for a `55 AA` / `PCIR` option ROM
matching the card's PCI vendor/device IDs.  Working tooling for this —
including the flash map driver and an FFS parser — is at
[[https://github.com/stevereaver/mbp41-nv50-backlight]].  Verified on kernel
7.1.x: nouveau accepts the extracted image via `config=NvBios=` and
initialises fully.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
